# Rotom Table private VPS environment example.
# Copy these values into your process manager environment or a real untracked
# .env file on the host. Keep real .env files, hostnames, credentials,
# and private campaign data out of Git.

NODE_ENV=production

# Bind Nitro to loopback when a same-host reverse proxy or access gate fronts the app.
# Change this only for a private network design you control.
NITRO_HOST=127.0.0.1
NITRO_PORT=3000

# Store campaign-owned JSON and the default live-play SQLite database outside the
# application checkout on the VPS.
ROTOM_CAMPAIGN_ROOT=/srv/rotom-table/campaign

# Optional: override the live-play SQLite database path.
# By default this is /srv/rotom-table/campaign/rotom-table.sqlite.
# Prefer the default; any override must still be private operator-controlled
# campaign storage outside the app checkout and included in backups with WAL sidecars.
# ROTOM_DB_PATH=/srv/rotom-table/campaign/rotom-table.sqlite

# Hosted production writes are a separate fail-closed opt-in for private hosts.
# Leave unset unless the instance has an outer access gate and should persist
# campaign JSON, campaign-owned reference override diffs such as Pokédex edits,
# and SQLite-backed live-play command results.
# The value must be exactly "1"; truthy words like "true" or "yes" are not valid.
# ROTOM_ENABLE_HOSTED_WRITES=1
